## Why This Is Asked
Assesses advanced AWS ABAC, cross-account governance, and policy-as-code in a multi-tenant data lake; targets practical use of IAM Identity Center, PrincipalTags, Lake Formation, and a GitOps deployment flow.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with session/principal tags
- Lake Formation fine-grained permissions
- Cross-account policy deployment (GitOps)
- Revocation latency and audits (CloudTrail, Config, Access Analyzer)

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": { "Federated": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:saml-provider/AWS_SSO" },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "tenant-A"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake",
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/tenant-A/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": { "s3:prefix": "tenant-A/" }
      }
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["lakeformation:GetDataLocation", "lakeformation:GetTable", "lakeformation:GrantPermissions", "glue:GetDatabase", "glue:GetTable"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": { "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "tenant-A" }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test revocation latency end-to-end? 
- How would you scale this across many tenants and regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical AWS multi-tenant isolation at scale, combining IAM session tags, Lake Formation, data catalog usage, and automated revocation; probes policy design, GitOps deployment, and testing.

## Key Concepts
- IAM role session tags
- Lake Formation permissions
- Data catalog integration
- Event-driven revocation with DynamoDB, EventBridge, Step Functions
- GitOps deployment of IAM policies
- Auditability: CloudTrail, Config, Access Analyzer

## Code Example
```json
// Trust policy snippet (AssumeRole requires matching tenant-id tag)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      },
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/PrincipalRoleForTenant"}
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Permission policy snippet (tenant-scoped S3 and Lake Formation actions)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-data/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
        "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-data/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["lakeformation:GetDataAccess"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"lakeformation:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cross-tenant leakage with automated CI checks?
- What monitoring would you add to detect revocation failures and alert on latency breaches?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design scalable multi-tenant data isolation using AWS IAM, Lake Formation, and S3 policies across multiple regions. It explores understanding of cross-region replication, governance controls, and auditability for SaaS applications.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped IAM roles with STS AssumeRole session tags
- Lake Formation permissions and data lake zone isolation
- S3 replication, encryption (SSE-KMS), and access boundaries
- Least-privilege access enforcement through bucket policies
- Auditing with CloudTrail, AWS Config, and Access Analyzer

## Code Example
```javascript
// Trust policy snippet for tenant role
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::${tenant_account_id}:role/TenantUser"},
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
    "Condition": {
      "StringEquals": {"aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${tenant_id}"},
      "StringLike": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${tenant_id}"}
    }
  }]
}

// S3 bucket policy for tenant isolation
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Deny",
    "Principal": "*",
    "Action": "s3:*",
    "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::datalake-bucket/*",
    "Condition": {
      "StringNotEquals": {"s3:prefix": ["${tenant_id}/*"]},
      "Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "true"}
    }
  }]
}
```
